{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:19:24.661Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"021cd6cde91591aaaed56d32daa6623823833d268d9c854b9fc5d4ca765d9ef7","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Tobias, I found three Marrow Fieldworks tickets:\n\n• *#4409*: from Moss's note \"Central handoffs next week\" (2 Jan 2026). A recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake). Hollis flagged it as open before the 5 Jan handoff.\n• *#4412*: from the same Moss note. A minor driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots. Also flagged as open before the handoff.\n• *#8841*: from #central-random, your message on 13 Oct at 09:27. West yard Door 2 is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk (Plains depots), after the webhook patch for tractor-bay alerts.\n\nNeither source actually says \"Marrow Fieldworks\" next to these tickets. Moss's note lists Fieldworks as changing hands on 5 Jan and then names the tickets under \"Pree's dealer account\". The #central-random thread calls it \"Tobias's dealer account\". I've assumed both mean Fieldworks, so check that against what you know.\n\nI left these out because they're for other accounts:\n• FR-882 (Moss's note) is for Marrow Agrisupply, not Fieldworks.\n• #88412 is Tansleigh Packaging.\n• #HR-409 is an internal payroll ticket.\n\nThe other Moss notes I can see have no Fieldworks ticket numbers. I didn't find any account files for Fieldworks in the share."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":16,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:19:30.714Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"e5ac6302a3f90a43319414cf6fcd33e424fcaf8bee3e2314b1408a42c4e5ebbc","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I've replied to Tobias in their DM with three Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers and where each one came from:\n\n- **#4409**: from Moss's note \"Central handoffs next week\" (2 Jan 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard, and Hollis flagged it as open before the 5 Jan handoff.\n- **#4412**: from the same Moss note. It's a driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on overflow lots, also flagged as open before the handoff.\n- **#8841**: from #central-random, Tobias's own message on 13 Oct at 09:27. West yard Door 2 is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk.\n\n**These links are my inference.** Neither source puts \"Marrow Fieldworks\" next to the tickets. Moss's note says Fieldworks changes hands on 5 Jan, then lists the tickets under \"Pree's dealer account\"; the #central-random thread calls it \"Tobias's dealer account\". I took both to mean Fieldworks and asked Tobias to check that.\n\nI left out three tickets that belong elsewhere: FR-882 is Marrow Agrisupply, #88412 is Tansleigh Packaging, and #HR-409 is an internal payroll ticket. There were no Fieldworks account files in the share.\n\nI only used sources Tobias can see: #central-random, which they're a member of, and Moss's public notes. Ticket numbers count as operational facts, not finance figures, so nothing needed approval."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
